  <p>Cosine is the share of the hypotenuse covered by the adjacent side: divide <span set:html={rich('[[b]]')} /> by <span set:html={rich('[[c]]')} /> to describe the triangle's shape. The formula <span set:html={rich('[[\\cos(A)=b/c]]')} /> needs only two measurements, the answer is always a dimensionless number between 0 and 1, and the rearranged forms <span set:html={rich('[[b=c\\cos(A)]]')} /> and <span set:html={rich('[[A=\\cos^{-1}(b/c)]]')} /> recover a missing side or the angle. Ladder, rafter, or textbook 3-4-5, the method never changes: identify the adjacent side, identify the hypotenuse, divide, and verify.</p>
